# Prepares the built fixture human-priest-mage-wounded-seed4-gate for the checks that load it (bd inc-10v7f).
# The old fixture, a .sav, held this state (bd inc-b4l3g.5, tools/check_held_mana.sh property 2): wizard mode
# on; a Mage level added to the Priest (Priest 1 / Mage 1, the base setup); Ignore Spell Failure on, because Cure Light Wounds
# fails on a roll the seed decides; the character wounded; every monster gone; the status bar reading Exploring.
# WOUNDED: a summoned giant rat bites while the character waits. The wait is cut short while a hostile is in
# view, so many waits are sent. The caller MUST export INCURSION_LOF_FORCE_ROLL=20 and
# INCURSION_FORCE_DAMAGE_ROLL=3 for the run: they make the rat bite for a known amount, so the wound is the
# same on every seed. Then every monster is cleared and the character searches once.
# Ruling V7-1: a fixture holds only the created character, so the checks that need the state make it here.
@include setup-human-priest-mage-seed4-gate.keys   # wizard on, Free Advancement, Priest 1 / Mage 1

w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*5
SPACE                   # Ignore Spell Failure
ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Animals"
@choose "giant rat"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@until "HP:" ESC
. . . . . . . . . .
. . . . . . . . . .
. . . . .

w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
s
